    "bookid": 44,
    "chapterId": 122,
    "fileId": 17850,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Adamantinomatous craniopharyngioma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Pankeratin (immunostaining for AE1/AE3 with light haematoxylin counterstain) reveals the few semiviable epithelial cells surrounding the wet keratin in this tumour, with the wet keratin seen as bluish-grey amorphous material on this immunostain (centre and at right).",
    "source": "Bette K. Kleinschmidt-DeMasters",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/44/122/17850.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/44/122/thumb_17850.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 49368,
    "bookid": 44,
    "chapterId": 122,
    "fileId": 17851,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Adamantinomatous craniopharyngioma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Wet keratin in these tumours undergoes dystrophic mineralization, although at this early stage of the process, the cell outlines are still faintly visible.",
    "source": "Bette K. Kleinschmidt-DeMasters",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/44/122/17851.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/44/122/thumb_17851.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 49369,
    "bookid": 44,
    "chapterId": 122,
    "fileId": 17853,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Adamantinomatous craniopharyngioma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Cholesterol debris, evidenced by cleft formation, can be found in some tumours; this is evidence of prior bleeding into the tumour.",
    "source": "Bette K. Kleinschmidt-DeMasters",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/44/122/17853.jpg",
